/E (1- All datasets are downloaded by hand from the ONAGRI-related data catalog website \(https://catalog.agridata.tn/en/dataset/\) for each category \(Forests, Animal production, Land development, Dams & Irrigated areas, Rainfall, Agricultural products\).)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
187 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 103 0 R
/E (2- The first portion of the R code fixes the major inconsistencies between Arabic and French naming conventions in the raw data and normalizes it using a reference dataset "Tunisia.csv" \(extracted from Tunisia GIS files, source: https://gadm.org/\).)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
188 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 103 0 R
/E (A unified region_id is added to join tabular data with spatial geometries. The output datasets are stored automatically as Clean data.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
189 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 103 0 R
/E (3- The second portion of the R code merges the clean data with the Tunisia_regions.shp boundary file using region_id. This attaches geometry to non-spatial data.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
